use crate::policy::Role;

pub(crate) fn print_auth_help(role: Option<Role>) {
    println!(
        "Authentication for {} (human-operator only: run as `admin auth setup`; AI roles must never invoke the admin group):\n\n  setup              Store a provider credential securely for one target role\n\nUsage: phasegent admin auth setup [--provider NAME] [--stdin] [--api-base <URL>] [--repository <O/R>] [--close-status-id <ID>] [--target-role ROLE]\n\nAn ordinary human Operator runs without a role and stores Admin by default. --target-role admin|orchestrator|executor|reviewer|explore selects the credential storage row and never the caller's identity or command visibility. A verified agent or a managed session without a role is rejected before any secret or storage access, even with --target-role. PHASEGENT_ROLE is a legacy marker only and grants no identity.\n\nOptions for setup:\n  --provider NAME     redmine, local, forgejo, or gitlab\n  --stdin             Read the credential from stdin\n  --api-base <URL>    Redmine REST address (machine-wide) or the Forgejo/GitLab instance root trusted for this role\n  --repository <O/R>  Redmine bootstrap/discovery repository, or the Forgejo/GitLab outside-Git repository default\n  --close-status-id <ID> Store the Redmine closed status\n  --target-role ROLE  Store the credential for admin, orchestrator, executor, reviewer, or explore (default Admin)\n\nA Forgejo or GitLab role's stored instance plus its own token are one trust boundary: an explicit --api-base must normalize exactly to that instance, and the stored repository is only the default outside Git. Per-operation --repository may name another repository on the same trusted instance; the server enforces the token's permissions. GitLab stores the instance root without /api/v4 and the full namespace/subgroup/project path.\n\nStable non-secret endpoint settings resolve CLI flags > PHASEGENT_* environment > TOML phasegent.toml (read-only overlay, absolute PHASEGENT_CONFIG_PATH override) > SQLite > defaults; `admin config set`/`clear` write SQLite only and a TOML value shadows until removed. Credentials stay in SQLite/env and are never stored in TOML. Redmine `admin workflow bootstrap` needs only the admin API key: built-in role users are found/created via admin and their keys stored locally in SQLite. Automatic issue-create bootstrap is internal system preparation with the admin credential (no caller admin authority, no fallback, no role switch), distinct from explicit `admin workflow bootstrap`. The Redmine REST address is machine-wide: `auth setup --api-base` and `admin config set redmine-api-base` store the one address every role shares and never create a per-role address. Credentials, provisioned identities, provider selection, and the Redmine close-status id stay role-scoped.\nThe role is a capability policy, not identity isolation; credentials must still be least-privilege.\nCredentials are never accepted as command-line arguments.\nProject IDs are invocation-only via --project-id and are never persisted.",
        role.map_or("all roles", Role::as_str)
    );
}
